������������� �������������� ������ ���������������������� ������������������ �������������� ��������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n1 Bokaro 61 \n2 Chatra 330 \n3 Deoghar 361 \n4 Dhanbad 419 \n5 Garhwa 353 \n6 Giridih 160 \n7 Godda 11 \n8 Gumla 142 \n9 Hazaribagh 886 \n10 Koderma 10 \n11 Latehar 251 \n12 Lohardaga 85 \n13 Palamu 453 \n14 Ramgarh 437 \n15 Ranchi 726 \n16 Sahebganj 2 \n17 SaraikelaKharsawan 12 \n18 West Singhbhum 230 "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|STARRED   |20", "t": "Schemes to Promote Rural Tourism in Rajasthan", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.†*20 \nANSWERED ON 04.12.2023 \n \nSCHEMES TO PROMOTE RURAL TOURISM IN RAJASTHAN \n \n†*20. SHRI SUMEDHANAND SARASWATI: \n  \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether rural tourism is essential for the economy of the country; \n(b) whether there is a strong potential for rural tourism market in \nRajasthan in the country; \n(c) if so, whether the Government is formulating any scheme for \nbringing improvement in various sectors in order to promote rural \ntourism; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the positive outcome achieved in this \nregard? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF TOURISM    (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n******* \n\n \nSTATEMENT IN R EPLY TO PARTS (a ) TO ( d) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.†*20 ANSWERED ON 04.12.2023 REGARDING SCHEMES \nTO PROMOTE RURAL TOURISM IN RAJASTHAN  BY SHRI \nSUMEDHANAND SARASWATI \n \n(a):  Yes, the rural tourism is contributing to  the economy of the \ncountry.  \n \n(b): Yes, t here is a strong potential for r ural tourism market in \nRajasthan keeping in view its heritage, traditions, vibrant and varied \nculture, craft religious practices, fairs and festivals.  \n \n(c) & (d): Recognizing the potential of rural tourism in the coun try, the \nMinistry of Tourism has formulated a “National Strategy and Roadmap \nfor Development of rural t ourism in India – An initiative towards \nAtmanirbhar Bharat”.  The strategy document focusses on the following \nkey pillars:- \n \n(i) Model Policies and Best Practices for Rural Tourism \n(ii) Digital Technologies and Platforms for Rural Tourism \n(iii) Developing Clusters for Rural Tourism \n(iv) Marketing Support for Rural Tourism \n(v) Capacity Building of Stakeholders \n(vi) Governance and Institutional Framework \n \n2. In addition to above, the St ate Government of Rajasthan has \ninformed that they have launched Rajasthan Rural Tourism Scheme, \n2022 in November 2022 for establishment of different types of tourism \nunits on rural agriculture and residential/Abadi land.  Key features of the \nScheme are as under: - \n \n(i) Rural t ourism units include – Agro Tourism Units, Carvan \nPark, Camping sites on agriculture land and Guest House on \nResidential/Abadi land. \n(ii) Rural Tourism units can be set up on agriculture land without \nany change in land use. \n\n(iii) 10% ground coverage and G+1 structure permissible under \nthe scheme for units on agriculture and other related \nactivities. \n(iv) Admissible benefits:  Exemption in Stamp Duty, 100% \nreimbursement of SGST for 10 years and subsidized loans \n(upto 9% interest subsidy). \n(v) So far 56 rural t ourism units have been established in \ndifferent districts of the State. \n \n3. Ministry of Tourism has also sanctioned the following project in \nthe State of Rajasthan under its PRASHAD Scheme:- \n(Rs. In crore) \nName of the Project \nYear of \nsanction \nApproved \ncost \nAmount \nreleased \nPhysical \nProgress \nIntegrated Development \nof Pushkar/ Ajmer \n2015-16 32.64 26.11 92% \n \nApart from above, Ministry of Tourism has sanctioned Central Financial \nAssistance amounting to Rs.40.00 lakh for celebration of Fa ir and \nFestival and events in the State of Rajasthan in 2014-15. \n \nMinistry of Tourism also identified Rural Circuit as one of the thematic \ncircuits under its Swadesh Darshan Scheme.  No project was sanctioned \nto the State Government of Rajasthan under Rura l Circuit  of the \nScheme. However, the Ministry has sanctioned four projects under other \ncircuits to the State Government of Rajasthan.  The details of these \nprojects are given at Annexure. \n \n******* \n\n     ANNEXURE \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (c ) & (d) OF L OK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.†*20 ANSWERED ON 04.12.2023 REGARDING SCHEMES \nTO PROMOTE RURAL TOURISM IN RAJASTHAN  BY SHRI \nSUMEDHANAND SARASWATI \n \nDetails of Projects sanctioned to the State Government of Rajasthan \nunder Swadesh Darshan Scheme \n(Rs. In Crore) \nS. \nNo. \nCircuit \nand Year \nof \nSanction \nProject Amount \nsanctio\nned \nAmount \nrelease\nd \nAmount \nutilized \nStatus Implementing \nAgency \n1.  Desert  \nCircuit \n \n2015-16 \nDevelopment of \nSambhar Lake \nTown and Other \nDestinations \n50.01 50.01 55.89 Complete Rajasthan \nTourism \nDevelopment \nCorporation \n(RTDC) \n2.  Krishna  \nCircuit \n \n2016-17 \nDevelopment of \nGovind Dev ji \ntemple (Jaipur), \nKhatu Shyam Ji \n(Sikar) and \nNathdwara \n(Rajsamand) \n75.80 72.01 77.49 Complete Rajasthan \nTourism \nDevelopment \nCorporation \n(RTDC) \n3.  Spiritual \nCircuit \n \n2016-17 \nDevelopment of \nSpiritual \nCircuit– \n'Development of \nChuru (Salasar \nBalaji)-Jaipur \n(Shri Samodke \nBalaji, Ghatke \nBalaji, \nBandheke \nBalaji)- \nViratnagar \n(Bijak, \nJainnasiya, \nAmbika \n87.05 72.23 75.03 Complete Rajasthan \nTourism \nDevelopment \nCorporation \n(RTDC) \n\nTemple)- \nBharatpur \n(Kaman \nRegion)- \nDholpur \n(Muchkund) - \nMehndipur \nBalaji- \nChittorgarh \n(Sanwaliyaji) \n4.  Heritage \n Circuit \n \n2017-18 \nDevelopment of \nHerit"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|STARRED   |200", "t": "Screening of Cancer", "head": "*29(510(17 2) ,1',$\n0,1,675< 2) +($/7+ $1' )$0,/< :(/)$5(\n'(3$570(17 2) +($/7+ 5(6($5&+\n/2. 6$%+$\n67$55(' 