\n52263.54\n160489.65\n21556.25\n61986.74\n56967.31\n67386.37\n111076.74\n47140.81\n49632.53\nWheat\nApr-22 to\n89145.11\n137908.81\n82471.03\n54152.01\n105674.56\n89731.66\n83806.48\n71963.24\n43017.79\n52940.41\n75010.12\n63763.82\n45226.97\n69135.35\n63579.86\n57001.76\n171926.79\n23458.73\n67830.28\n61150.52\n73658.90\n120809.50\n52365.24\n52977.25\n\n\n-2-\n+$eRic+\nagaur\n26 ma\n27 In\n28 ljsamand\na29\nSikar\nirohi\n32 Tonk\n33 Fdaipur\nTotal\n121352.07\n68384.55\n34165.72\n45888.16\n43511.64\n90389.85\n39287.47\n51455.44\n120223.71\n2276790.80\n131189.61\n75298.37\n36793.38\n50335.07\n47771.25\n98045.87\n43347.44\n56208.95\n131505.67\n2479201.96\n\n\nANNEXURE-II\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) & (b) OF THE UNSTARRED\nQUESTION NO.563 FOR ANSWER ON 06.12.2023 IN THE LOK SABHA.\nNFSA Beneficiaries in Rajasthan Getting Benefits under PM-GKAY\nS. No. 1 District I No. of NFSA Beneficiaries\nml\n2\n3\nm4\n5\n6\n7\n8\nm9\nI\n1\nI\n3\n1\nG\n1\n1\n1\nI\n2\n1\nJODHPUR\nKARAULI\nKOTA\n15,69,318\n24,27,330\n14,04,41 1\n9,3 1,984\n18,90, 1 14\n16,06,274\n14,79,564\n12,97, 1 13\n7,49,532\n9,27,425\n13,28,469\n11,15,067\n8,52,904\n11,73,602\n11,75,412\n9,94,448\n30,69,519\n4,04,385\n12,09,272\n10,46,271\n13,27,940\n21 ,74,467\n+69,45, 1\nW2\n\n\n-2-\n25\n26\n27\n28\n29\n30\n31\n32\n33\nNAGAUR\nPALI\nPRATAPGARH\nRAJSAMAND\nSAWAI MADHOPUR\nSIKAR\nSIROHI\nTONK\nUDAIPUR\n23,48,348\n13,38,394\n6,29,779\n8,71,455\n8,67,565\n17,47,005\n7,55,964\n9,82,890\n22,44,367\nGrand Total 4,38,06,795\n+++++\n"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |564", "t": "Safety Rules of Private Trains", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 564 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.12.2023 \n \nSAFETY RULES OF PRIVATE TRAINS \n564. SHRI MANICKAM TAGORE B. :  \n  \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether it is a fact that the Railways has tightened safety rules \nin the operation of private trains and coaches and if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n \n(b) whether it is a fact that the Railways has issued fresh \nguidelines for catering services and security checks and if so, \nthe details in this regard; \n \n(c) whether the decision came a month after a private coach \ntransporting pilgrims went up in flames in Madurai, leaving nine \npassengers dead and a few others injured; and \n \n(d) if so, the facts and details thereof? \n \n \n    ANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n***** \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO 564 BY SHRI MANICKAM TAGORE B . TO \nBE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 06.12.2023 REGARDING SAFETY \nRULES OF PRIVATE TRAINS \n \n(a) to (d):  There are uniform safety rules i.e. General and Subsidiary \nRules for the operation of all trains, including private trains, on the \nIndian Railways network. \nAs a preventive safety measure, the following policy instructions \nwere issued on 07.09.2023 with respect to provision of catering \nservices in Full Tariff Rates (FTR) trains: \n \n Catering facilities in all coaches/trains etc. booked on Full Tariff \nRates (FTR) to be arranged by IRCTC, except for trains booked with \nPantry Car.  \n \n In case of trains booked with Pantry Car under FTR, booking parties \nmay either avail the catering facilities through IRCTC or provide the \ncatering facilities using pantry, strictly in ter ms of the existing \ninstructions, prohibiting flame based cooking in pantry cars.  \n \nIt is further stated that, ‘Police’ and ‘Public Order’ are State \nsubjects under the Seventh Schedule to the Constitution of India and, \ntherefore, State Governments are respo nsible for prevention, \ndetection, registration and investigation of crime and maintenance of \nlaw and order on Railways through their law enforcement agencies viz. \nGovernment Railway Police (GRP)/District Police. Railway Protection \n\nForce (RPF) supplements t he efforts of GRP/District Police to provide \nbetter protection and security to railway property, passenger area and \npassengers and for matter connected therewith. \n As per Section 164 of the Railways Act, 1989 ‘Unlawfully bringing \ndangerous goods on a railw ay’ is a punishable offence. Extensive \nchecks/Special Drives are conducted on trains and station premises to \ntake action against offenders carrying inflammable substances, \nexplosives etc. as per law. Intensive special drives/operations are also \nconducted i n trains during festival seasons, rush periods to prevent \ncarriage of fire crackers and offenders are taken up under the legal \nprovisions. Also, massive awareness campaigns are conducted by \ndistributing leaflets, pasting of posters, making announcements \nthrough Public Address System, loud hailers, Nukkad Nataks, Media \ni.e. print media/electronic media and social media etc. to make \npassengers aware about the consequences of carrying \ninflammable/explosive articles in trains and railway premises. \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |565", "t": "Promotion of Industrial Activities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \nDEPARTMENT FOR PROMOTION OF INDUSTRY AND INTERNAL TRADE \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 565. \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, THE 06th DECEMBER, 2023. \n \nPROMOTION OF INDUSTRIAL ACTIVITIES \n \n565.  SHRI MANOJ KOTAK: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY be pleased to state: \n                                  वाणिज्य  एवं उद्योग मंत्री \n(a)  whether it is a fact that the Government is  providing support for promotion of \nIndustrial activities across the country; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)  the details of all industrial and manufacturing units set up in Maharashtra; \n \n(d)  the steps taken by the Government to promote industries in Maharashtra; and \n \n(e)  the number of Special Economic Zones  (SEZs) in Maharashtra along with their \nstatus? \n \nANSWER \n \nवाणिज्य  एवं उद्योग मंत्रालय में राज्य मंत्री (श्री सोम प्रकाश)   \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRI SOM PARKASH) \n \n(a) & (b): The Government of India has taken up several initiatives/announced schemes for \nthe promotion of industries and industrial activity across the country. These  include \nMake in India initiative, Industrial Development Schemes for Himachal  Pradesh, \nUttarakhand, Jammu and Kashmir, and Ladakh, North East Industrial \nDevelopment Scheme and initiatives for promoting Ease of Doing Business, etc. \n \nThe other measures for the promotion of industrial activity include Atmanirbhar  \nBharat packages, introduction of Production  Linked Incentive (PLI) Scheme,  \ninvestment opportunities under National Infrastructure Pipeline (NIP) and National \nMonetisation Pipeline (NMP), India Industrial Land Bank (IILB), Industrial Park \nRating System (IPRS), launch of the National Single Window  System (NSWS), \ndevelopment of National Industrial Corridors, etc. An institutional mechanism to \nfast-track investments  has also been put in place, in  the form of Project \nDevelopment Cells (PDCs) in all the concerned Ministries/  Departments of \nGovernment of India. \n(c) & (d): ‘Industry’ is primarily a State subject. The Union Government supplements efforts \nof States/UTs through various measures to promote industrialization in the \ncountry. In Maharashtra, there are a total of 8,36,082 MSME manufacturing units  \nregistered under Udyog Aadhaar Memorandum (UA M) and 38,418 large scale  \nunits registered under the Factories Act, 1948. \n \n(e): In the State of Maharashtra, a total of 44 Special Economic Zones (SEZs) are \nnotified and 38 SEZs are operational. The details of these SEZs are at Annexure. \n \n********* \n\nANNEXURE \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (e) OF THE LOK SABHA  USTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 565 FOR ANSWER ON 06.12.2023. \n \nSl. \nNo. \nName of the \nSEZ \nLocation Type of SEZ Area \n(hectare) \nSEZ Status \n1 SEEPZ Special  \nEconomic Zone \nMumbai, Maharashtra Multi Product \n(Electronics and \nGems and          Jewellery) \n44.93 Notified &  \nOperational \n2 Serum Bio - \npharma Park \nVillage Hadapsar/  \nManjri, District Pune,  \nMaharashtra \nPharmaceuticals & \nBiotechnology \n16.01 Notified &  \nOperational \n3 EON Kharadi  \nInfrastructure \nPrivate Limited \nTaluka Haveli, \nDistrict Pune,  \nMaharashtra \nIT/ITES 18 Notified &  \nOperational \n4 Maharashtra \nIndustrial \nDevelopment \nCorporation \nShendre Industrial \nArea, District  \nAurangabad, \nMaharashtra \nEngineering & \nElectronics \n57.22 Notified &  \nOperational \n5 WIPRO \nLimited \nHinjawadi District, \nPune, Maharashtra \nIT/ITES 20 Notified &  \nOperational \n6 Maharashtra \nIndustrial \nDevelopment \nCorporation \nVillage Krushnoor,  \nTaluka Naigaon,  \nDistrict Nanded,  \nMaharashtra \nPharmaceutica ls 150 Notified &  \nOperational \n7 Syntel International \nPrivate Limited \nTalwade Software  \nPark, District Pune,  \nMaharashtra \nIT/ITES 16 Notified &  \nOperational \n8 The Manjri  Stud \nFarm Private \nLimited \nVillage Phursungi,  \nTaluka Haveli, Pune, \nMaharashtra \nIT/ITES 15.79 Notified &  \nOperational \n9 HGP \nCommunity Pvt. \nLtd. \nVillage Powai,  \nDistrict Mumbai, \nMaharashtra \nIT/ITES 3.62 Notified &  \nOperational \n10 Wockhardt \nBioPharma \nLimited \nShendre Five Star  \nIndustrial Area , \nAurangabad District, \nMaharashtra \nPharmaceutica ls 107 Notified &  \nOperational \n11 Infosys \nTechnologies \nLimited \nRajiv Gandhi Infotech \nPark, Phase –II, village \nMann, Tal. \nMulshi, District Pune, \nMaharashtra \nIT/ITES 31.49 Notified &  \nOperational \n12 Maharashtra \nAirport \nDevelopment \nCompany \nLimited (MADC) \nNagpur (MIHAN),  \nDistrict Nagpur,  \nMaharashtra \nMulti-product 1597.16 Notified &  \nOperational \n13 Maharashtra \nIndustrial \nDevelopment \nCorporation \nLimited (MIDC) \n \n \n \nRajiv Gandhi Infotech \nPark, Hinjawadi,  Phase-\nIII, District  Pune, \nMaharashtra \nIT/ITES 223 Notified &  \nOperational \n\n14 Magarpatta \nTownship \nDevelopment and \nConstruction \nCompany Ltd. \nMagarpatta City,  \nVillage Hadapsar, \nTaluka Haveli,  \nDistrict Pune,  \nMaharashtra \nElectronics \nHardware and  \nSoftware including \ninformation \ntechnology enab"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |566", "t": "Sanctioned Railway Projects in Karnataka", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 566 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.12.2023 \n  \nSANCTIONED RAILWAY PROJECTS IN KARNATAKA \n \n566. SHRI S. MUNISWAMY: \n  \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of sanctioned railway projects from May 2019 till date \nfor the Kolar Lok Sabha Constituency of Karnataka; \n \n(b) the timeline to complete the sanctioned Broad Guage line between \nMarikuppam and Kuppam; \n \n(c) the details of projects in the pipeline from the Railways for the Lok \nSabha Constituency of Kolar in Karnataka; and \n \n(d) the total expenditure from May 2019 till date for the Kolar Lok \nSabha Constituency in Karnataka? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n***** \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 566 BY SHRI S. MUNISWAMY TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 06.12.2023  REGARDING  SANCTIONED \nRAILWAY PROJECTS IN KARNATAKA \n \n(a) and (b): Railway projects are sanctioned and taken up Zonal Railway -\nwise and not State -wise/constituency-wise as the Indian Railway’s \nprojects may span across various State boundaries. From April, 2019 to \ntill date, one new line project between Dharwad and Belgaum via Kittur \n(73 Km) and one doubling project between Jokkatte and Thokur (2 Km) \nfalling fully/partly in the State of Karnataka have been sanctioned. \nHowever, 2 Road Safety works i.e. Road Over Bridge (ROB) have been \nsanctioned in Kolar Lok Sabha Constituency of Karnataka from April, \n2019 to till date. \n \nMarikuppam -Kuppam new line (24 Km) project falls in Karnataka \n(length: 6 Km) and Andhra Pradesh (length: 18 Km). Land acquisition for \nthe project has been taken up. The Pro ject involves acquisition of 70.14 \nacre land {including 49.70 acre land of Bharat Gold Mines Limited \n(BGML)} in Karnataka and 255.24 acre land in Andhra Pradesh. So far, \ntotal 70.14 acre land in Karnataka and 196.5 acre land in Andhra \nPradesh handed over b y the respective State Government to Railways. \nLand acquisition of balance 58.74 acre land in Andhra Pradesh has been \ntaken up. In Karnataka portion works have been taken up.  \n \nThe completion of any Railway project depends on various factors \nlike quick land  acquisition  by  State  Government,  forest  clearance  by  \nofficials of forest  department,  shifting  of  infringing  utilities,  statutory  \n…2/- \n \n \n\n-2- \nclearances from various authorities, geological and topographical \nconditions of area, law and order  situation in the area of project site, \nnumber of working months in a year for particular project site due to \nclimatic conditions etc.  All these factors affect the completion time of \nthe project. With above constraints, every effort is being made to \nexecute the project(s) expeditiously. \n \n(c): Railway projects are sanctioned and taken up Zonal Railway -wise \nand not State -wise/constituency-wise as the Indian Railway’s projects \nmay span across various State boundaries. However, as  on 01.04.2023, \n31 projects (21 new lines and 10 Doubling) of 3,866 km length, costing               \n`47,346 crore falling fully/partly in the State of Karnataka are in \nplanning/approval/construction stage. A n expenditure of `15,881 crore \nhas been incurred upto March 2023.  These include:- \n \n • 21 New Line Projects of total length 2,583 km at a cost of `33,218 \ncrore, out of which 366 Km length has been commissioned and an \nexpenditure of `6,019 crore has been incurred upto March 2023. \n \n • 10 Doubling Projects of total length 1,283 km at a cost of `14,128 \ncrore, out of which 780 Km length has been commissioned and an \nexpenditure of `9,862 crore has been incurred upto March 2023. \n \n(d): Railway infrastructure projects falling fully/partly in  the State of \nKarnataka are covered under South Western Railway (SWR), Central \nRailway (CR), Southern Railway (SR) and South Central Railway (SCR) \nZone of Indian Railway. Zone -wise and Year -wise details of all Railway \nprojects including  cost,  expenditure  and  outlay  are  made available in  \n…3/- \n \n\n-3- \n \npublic domain on Indian Railways website i.e.  \nwww.indianrailways.gov.in > Ministry of Railways >Railway Board \n>About Indian Railways > Railway Board Directorates >Finance (Budget) \n>Rail Budget/Pink Book (Year)> Railway wise Works Machinery and \nRolling Stock Programme. \n \nSince 2014, there has been substantial increase in fund allocation \nand commensurate commissioning of projects across Indian Railways. \nAverage Annual Budget allocation for Infrastructure projects & safety \nworks, falling fully/ partly in State of Karnataka, during 2014-19 has been \nenhanced to `2,702  crore per year which is 224% more than Average \nAnnual Budget allocation of `835 crore per year during 2009 -14. The \nallocation has increased to `3,386 crore in Financial Year 2019 -20 (306% \nmore than the A"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |567", "t": "Cancellation of Passenger Trains", "head": "   \n \n GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.567 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.12.2023 \n \nCANCELLATION OF PASSENGER TRAINS \n \n567. DR. M.P. ABDUSSAMAD SAMADANI:  \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to State: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware of the difficulties faced by local \npassengers in the Shoranur -Mangalore sector of the Palakkad \ndivision in Southern Railway due to the cancellation of passenger \ntrains and time schedule of the trains and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether the Government has plans to reinstate the cancelled trains \nor increase unreserved coaches in the existing express trains to \nresolve the congestion in existing  passenger trains and unreserved \ncoaches of express trains and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government is aware of the delays to existing trains \ncaused by the newly introduced Vande Bharat trains; and  \n \n(d) if so, the remedial measures taken by the Railways in this regard? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND  \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n (SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW)  \n \n(a) to (d) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n                                                                        \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 567 ASKED BY DR. M.P. ABDUSSAMAD SAMADANI TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 06.12.2023 REGARDING CANCELLATION OF \nPASSENGER TRAINS \n \n(a) & (b) Indian Railways have undertaken rationalization of  time table in a \nscientific manner with the assistance of IIT -Bombay. The exercise has \nbeen undertaken inter alia to provide for better passenger safety by \ncreating maintenance corridor blocks, generation of additional paths and \nminimizing conflicts in exi sting time table to improve punctuality. The \nexercise, inter-alia, necessitated rationalization of train services including \nthe discontinuation of 06496 Kozhikode -Shoranur Unreserved Express \nSpecial and partial discontinuation of 06495 Thrisur -Kozhikode Unreserved \nExpress Special between Shoranur -Kozhikode. However, for the \nconvenience of the passengers using the services of 06496 Special \nExpress, the timings of 16607 Kannur - Coimbatore Express has been \nrevised so as to operate to similar schedule. Similar ly, for the passengers \nusing the services of 06495 Thrisur-Kozhikode Unreserved Express Special, \nthe timings of 16608 Coimbatore – Kannur Express have been revised so as \nto depart Shoranur at 16:20 hrs. \nFurther, to cater to the needs of General class passengers, 5 pairs of trains \nviz. 16303/16304 Ernakulam -Thiruvananthapuram Vanchinad Express, \n16305/16306 Ernakulam - Kannur Express, 16307/16308 Alappuzha - Kannur \nExpress, 16301/16302 Shoranur - Thiruvananthapuram Venad Express and \n16649/16650 Mangaluru -Nagercoil Parasuram Express have each been \npermanently augmented by one General class coach. These are in addition \nto the temporary augmentations undertaken to meet the extra rush of \npassengers.  \n(c) & (d) Vande Bharat Express services run as per their scheduled Time \nTable. Operation of these services does not lead to delay in operations of \nother train services on the Shoranur –Mangaluru sector. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |568", "t": "Ongoing/Pending Railway Projects in Jalpaiguri", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 568 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.12.2023 \n \nONGOING/PENDING RAILWAY PROJECTS IN JALPAIGURI \n  \n568.  DR. JAYANTA KUMAR ROY: \n           \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of railway stations in the Jalpaiguri Parliamentary Constituency;  \n(b)  the details of railway projects/works planned, ongoing and pending in the \nsaid Constituency;  \n(c)  whether the Government has any plans for development of these railway \nstations with modern infrastructure, if so, the details thereof;  \n(d)  whether the Government has any plans to augment the rail \nnetwork/connectivity and train services in the Jalpaiguri constituency; and  \n(e)  if so, the steps being taken by the Government in this regard? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COMMUNICATIONS AND \nELECTRONICS & INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n \n(SHRI ASHWINI VAISHNAW) \n (a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n*****  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 568 BY DR. JAYANTA KUMAR ROY TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 06.12.2023 REGARDING  ONGOING/ \nPENDING RAILWAY PROJECTS IN JALPAIGURI. \n  \n(a): 34 railway stations which fall in the Jalpaiguri Par liamentary \nConsituency are Belakoba, Rani Nagar Jalpaiguri, New Jalpaiguri, \nAmbari Falakata, Jalpaiguri, Kadabari, Mandalghat, Kashiabari, Mohit \nNagar, Jalpaiguri Road, New Domohani, New Mainaguri, Betgara, \nAltagram, Dhupguri, Kolaigram, Salbari, Begrakot,  Oodlabari, Damdim, \nNew Mal Jn, Chalsa, Nagrakata, Caron, Banarhat, Mal Bazar, \nBoradighi, Lataguri, Domohni, Mayanaguri Road, New Changrabandha, \nChangrabandha, Neoranandi and Bhotepatti. \n \n(b) to (e): Railway projects are sanctioned Zonal Railway wise not \nParliamentary Constituency wise as Railway projects may span across \nParliamentary constituencies. Jalpaiguri Parliamentary Constituency \nfalls in the State of West Bengal. As on 01.04.2023, 44 railway projects \n(16 New line, 04 Gauge Conversion  and 24 Doubling) of total length of \n4,209 km, costing 50,915 crore, falling fully/partly in the state of \nWest Bengal are in planning/approval/construction stage,  out  of  \nwhich, 2,033 km length has been commissioned  and an expenditure of \n23,298 crore has been incurred upto March, 2023. During 2014 -23, \n1137 Km sections (113 km of New line, 151 Km of Gauge Conversion \nand 873 km of Doubling) have been commissioned in State of West \nBengal at an average rate 126.33 km per year. \nMinistry of Railways has launched ‘Amrit Bharat Station \nScheme’ for development of Railway stations on Indian Railways. \n\n\nThis scheme envisages development of stations on a continuous \nbasis with a long -term approach.  Under the schem e, 1309 \nRailway Stations on Indian Railways including 6 stations namely, \nNew Jalpaiguri Junction, Dhupguri, Haldibari, Jalpaiguri, \nJalpaiguri Road and New Mal Junction in the Jalpaiguri \nParliamentary constitutency have been identified for \ndevelopment as Am rit Bharat Stations.  \nThis scheme involves preparation of Master Plans and their \nimplementation in phases to improve the amenities at the \nstations like improvement of station access, circulating areas, \nwaiting halls, toilets, lift/escalators as necessary, c leanliness, \nfree Wi -Fi, kiosks for local products through schemes like ‘One \nStation One Product’, better passenger information systems, \nExecutive Lounges, nominated spaces for business meetings, \nlandscaping etc., keeping in view the necessity and requireme nt \nat each sation. The scheme also envisages improvement of \nbuilding, integrating the station with both sides of the city, \nmultimodal integration, amenities for Divyangjans, sustainable \nand environment friendly solutions, provision of ballastless \ntracks, ‘ Roof Plazas’ as per necessity, phasing and feasibility and \ncreation of city centres at the station in the long term.  \nAt present, New Jalpaiguri station is being catered by 146 train \nservices.  Besides, introduction of new trains/ extension and increase \nin frequency of services,  to enhance train connectivity, is an on -going \nprocess on Indian Railways subject to operational feasibility, traffic \njustification, resource availability, etc.  \n\nVarious steps taken by the Government for effective and speedy \nimplementation of rail projects include (i) substantial increase in \nallocation of funds, (ii) delegation of powers at field level, (iii) close \nmonitoring of progress of project at various levels (iv) regular follow up \nwith State Governments and concerned authoritie s for expeditious \nland acquisition, forestry and Wildlife clearances and for resolving \nother issues pertaining to projects.  \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |569", "t": "Poor Quality of Wi-Fi", "head": "1 \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS  \nDEPARTMENT OF TELECOMMUNICATIONS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 569 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 6TH DECEMBER, 2023 \n \nPOOR QUALITY OF WI-FI \n \n†569.  SHRI NABA KUMAR SARANIA: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the reasons for the poor quality of Wi -Fi provided to MPs at their accommodation in Delhi \nand their homes in their respective constituencies; and \n \n(b)  whether any necessary steps have been taken to improve its quality and if so, the details \nthereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR COMMUNICATIONS \n(SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN) \n \n(a)&(b) Internet services including  Wi-Fi are being provided to Hon’ble Members of \nParliament (MPs) in Delhi with regular proactive maintenance to maintain the quality. \n \n With regard to broadband connections provided by BSNL, it is increasingly moving towards \nproviding Fiber to the Home (FTTH) connections. A dedicated portal \nhttps://selfcare.bsnl.co.in/SansadSeva  for resolving complaints of Hon’ble MPs has been deployed.  \nAlso, nodal officers of BSNL in each of the Telecom Circles  are to ensure immediate redressal of \nthe complaints raised by Hon’ble MPs. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |57", "t": "Multiple Entry and Multiple Exit (MEME) in NEP", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION  \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION  \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No-57 \nANSWERED ON- 04/12/2023 \nMULTIPLE ENTRY AND MULTIPLE EXIT (MEME) IN NEP \n57. SHRI SRIDHAR KOTAGIRI: \n Will the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government is considering to  develop new options for Multiple Entry \nand Multiple Exit (MEME) in NEP to resolve hurdles in managing  MEME in several \nareas; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION  \n(DR. SUBHAS SARKAR) \n(a) to (c): National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 seeks to reform the Higher Education \nsystem by providing, among other things, flexibility to students in terms of  choice of \nsubjects to study and academic pathways. A creative combination of  disciplines for \nstudy with multiple entry and exit points is one of the major recommendations of NEP, \n2020. \n \n Accordingly, the University Grants Commission (UGC) has issued G uidelines \nfor Multiple Entry and Exit  in Academic Programmes offered in  Higher Education \nInstitutions on 29.07.2021. These guidelines are available at https://www.ugc.gov.in/e-\nbook/GL%20Multipe%20Entry%20Exit.pdf.   \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |570", "t": "Funding to Training Center under SAMARTH Scheme", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 570 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.12.2023 \n \nFUNDING TO TRAINING CENTER UNDER SAMARTH SCHEME \n \n \n570. SHRI RAJENDRA AGRAWAL: \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of TEXTILES वस्त्र मंत्री \nbe pleased to state : \n \n(a) whether the Government provides separate funding to each training center under the SAMARTH \nScheme and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(b) the details of the number of training programmes conducted in the country particularly in the State \nof Uttar Pradesh under the said scheme; and  \n \n(c) the number of beneficiaries trained so far and those provided with placements under the said scheme \nfrom the State of Uttar Pradesh? \n \n \n \n \nउत्तर \nANSWER \nवस्त्र राज्‍ य मंत्री (श्रीमती दर्शना जरदोर्) \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR TEXTILES  \n (SMT. DARSHANA JARDOSH) \n \n(a): Under SAMARTH, the flagship skilling scheme of Ministry of Textiles, training target to \nImplementing Partners (IPs) is allocated based upon assessing the capacity & adequacy of training \ncentres, requirement of skilled manpower for captive placement and employee strength. However, \nfunding of the training programme under the scheme is based on the per trainee hourly rates provided in \nthe Common Norms prescribed by Ministry of Skill Development & Entrepreneurship and relea sed \ndirectly to the IPs based on the physical progress of training programme. \n \n(b): Details of number of training programmes conducted in the country and in the State of Uttar \nPradesh under the scheme are as under: \n(as on 29.11.2023) \n No. of operational training \ncentres \nNo. of beneficiaries trained & \nassessed (passed) \nPan India 1,955 2,32,362 \nUttar Pradesh 286 30,369 \n  Data Source: MIS \n \n(c): Details of beneficiaries trained and those provided with placement under Samarth in Uttar Pradesh \nis given below: - \nSector  No. of beneficiaries trained & \nassessed (passed) \nNo. of beneficiaries provided \nplacement \nOrganized Sector 17,385 10,877 \nTraditional Sector  12,984 5,480* \nTotal  30,369 16,357 \n*The training programme  conducted in traditional sectors (viz. Handloom, Handicraft, Jute and Silk) \ncourses is also having a provision for self-employment.  \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |571", "t": "Active Coal Blocks", "head": "1 \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COAL \n  \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 571 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.12.2023 \n  \nActive Coal Blocks \n  \n571. SHRI M. BADRUDDIN AJMAL: \n  \nWill the Minister of COAL be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the details including the number of Coal blocks presently active in the country, State-wise; \n(b) the quantum of revenue/amount earned from Coal blocks across the country during the last five \nyears; and \n(c) the details of revenue along with the process of auction, block and year-wise?  \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS, COAL AND MINES \n(SHRI PRALHAD JOSHI)  \n  \n(a):  The number of functional mines in the country as on 01.04.2023, state-wise, are as under:   \n  \nState/ Union Territory (UT) Functional Coal Mines \nWB 71 \nJharkhand 119 \nMP 59 \nUP 5 \nChhattisgarh 51 \nMaharashtra 56