 365 354 29 29 - - \n23 Mizoram 36 38 96 96 - - \n24 Nagaland 297 299 168 168 - - \n25 Odisha 11,205 7,265 1,74"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |794", "t": "Rental Housing in Urban Areas", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 794 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON DECEMBER 07, 2023 \n \n                                    RENTAL HOUSING IN URBAN AREAS \n \nNO. 794. SHRI GNANATHIRAVIAM S.:     \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government proposes to provide rental housing in urban \nareas for migrants under Social Rental Housing Scheme; and \n(b) if so, the details thereof? \n \n          ANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE) \n \n(a)  & (b): Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs (MoHUA) has launched \nAffordable Rental Housing Complexes (ARHCs) as a sub- scheme of \nPradhan Mantri Awas Yojana -  Urban (PMAY -U) to provide dignified \nliving to urban migrants/poor near their workplace. This scheme is \nbeing implemented through two models as under:  \nModel-1: Utilizing existing Government funded vacant houses \nconstructed under Jawaharlal Nehru National Urban Renewal \nMission (JNNURM) and Rajiv Awas Yojana (RAY) to convert into \nARHCs through Public Private Partnership (PPP) or by Public \nAgencies, \nModel-2: Construction, Operation & Maintenance of ARHCs by \nPublic/Private Entities on their own available vacant land.  \nUnder Model-1 of the scheme, 5,648 houses have been converted into \nARHCs from States/Union Territories ( UTs) of Gujarat, Rajasthan, \nUttarakhand, Chandigarh and Jammu & Kashmir.  Under Model -2 of \nthe scheme, so far, proposals for construction of 82,273 new ARHC \nunits have been sanctioned, out of which construction of 48,113 \nARHC units are in progress in different States.   \n*****\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |795", "t": "Construction of Petrochemical Complex", "head": " \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 795 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 7 th December, 2023 \n \n  Construction of Petrochemical Complex  \n  \n†795. SHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE: \n \nपे\u0000ोिलयम और \u0000ाक ृितक गैस मं\u0000ी \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has received proposals from public representatives of \nMaharashtra and Vidarbha Economic Development Council (VED) for conducting \nfeasibility study for construction of Petrochemical complex in Vidarbha region; \n(b) if so, the details thereof as on date, date-wise; \n(c) whether the Government has taken or proposed to take any steps for the \nconstruction of Petrochemical complex in the said region, especially in Nagbhid in \ntribal dominated Parliamentary Constituency of Gadchiroli; and \n(d) if so, the updated status thereof? \n \nANSWER \nपे\u0000ोिलयम एवं \u0000ाक ृितक गैस मं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000यमं\u0000ी (\u0000ी रामे\u0000र तेली) \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PETROLEUM & NATURAL \nGAS \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n \n(a) to (b): Government has received representations on this subject from public \nrepresentatives from the State of Maharashtra in January, February, April, May, June, \nJuly and November 2021, in February 2022 and in March 2023.  \n \n(c) & (d): No Sir. \n \n********* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |796", "t": "Safe Operations of Aircrafts", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 796\n(To be answered on the 7th December 2023)\n \nSAFE OPERATIONS OF AIRCRAFTS\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) the details of accidents involving civilian aircrafts/helicopters along with\nthe loss of life and property reported during the last three years and the\ncurrent year, airline, location and year-wise;\n \n(b) whether the Government has conducted investigations into these accidents,\nand if so, the details and the findings thereof along with the compensation\npaid  to families of the victims and the parameters being adopted; and\n \n(c) the remedial steps taken or being taken by the Government to avert such\naccidents and for safe operations of aircrafts/helicopters in the country?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a)The details of accidents involving civilian aircraft/ helicopters during the\nlast three years and current year including airline, location, extent of damage\nand loss of life is enclosed as Annexure-A\n \n(b) The investigation in respect of all the accidents pertaining to civilian\nregistered aircraft and helicopters has been ordered by Aircraft Accident\nInvestigation Bureau (AAIB) as per the Aircraft (Investigation of Accidents &\nincidents) Rules, 2017. The final investigation reports of all concluded\ninvestigations including the findings have been published on the AAIB website\n(https://aaib.gov.in)\n \nPayment of compensation to the victims or families of victims in case of death\nor bodily injury to the passenger caused by air accident/incident is governed\nby the provisions of Carriage by Air Act, 1972. The concerned airline\ndischarges its liability of payment of compensation as per provision of the said\n796. SHRI G.M. SIDDESHWAR\n be pleased to state:-\n (GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD))\n\nAct.\n \n(c) DGCA has a robust mechanism of prevention of such accidents. Following\nsteps are taken by DGCA on a regular basis to prevent the accidents:\n \n(i)A systematic safety oversight process is in place for monitoring the\ncompliance of Rules and Civil Aviation Requirements which includes\nsurveillances, spot check and regulatory audits. In addition special audits are\nalso carried out as per the risk perceived.\n \n(ii)DGCA publishes Annual Surveillance Plan (ASP) on their website. Each\ndirectorate conduct surveillance/spot checks in their respective technical areas\nas per the ASP.\n \n(iii)Findings of audits, surveillances & spot checks are followed up with the\nconcerned operator for compliance. The observations are closed after due\nverification. Further the compliance of the action taken by the operator is\nverified during the next audit/surveillance\n \n(iv)In case of any violations/ non- compliance to regulations detected during\naudit/surveillance, enforcement action, including financial penalty is imposed\nby the DGCA.\n \n(v)Accident/incident data of India is regularly analyzed. Based on the analysis,\nthe information disseminated in Safety Circulars etc.\n \n(vi)Recommendations emanating from the investigation reports of accident/\nincident are implemented to prevent incidents.\n \n*****\n\nAnnexure - A \nS \nNo \nOccurrence \nType \n(Accident/ \nSerious \nIncident)  \nDetails of Occurrence (Airline, Aircraft \nType, Registration, Date, Place, etc.  Loss of Life \n2020 \n1 Accident      Chimse Aviation Pvt. Ltd., Cessna 172, VT-CAF, \n03.01.2020, Dhana \n(Fatal-02) \n2 Accident      Govt. of Jharkhand, Super Blanik Glider, VT-GLE, \n03.02.2020, Dumka \n(Fatal-01) \n3 Accident      Govt. Aviation Training Institute, Cessna 152, VT-\nENF, 08.06.2020, Bhubaneshwar \n(Fatal-02) \n4 Accident M/s Indigo, Airbus A320, VT-IJT, 14.06.2020, Cochin  \n5 Accident M/s Jindal Steel & Power Ltd, Cessna Citation XLS, \nVT-JSS, 28.06.2020, Vijayanagar \n \n6 Accident      M/s Air India Express, Boeing B737-800, VT-AXH, \n07.08.2020, Kozhikode \n(Fatal-21) \n7 Accident      M/s IGRUA, TB20, VT-IGE, 21.09.2020, Azamgarh, \nUP \n(Fatal-01) \n2021 \n1 Accident M/s Air India Express, B737-800, VT-GHE, \n20.02.2021, Vijayawada \n \n2 Accident M/s Pinnacle Air Pvt Ltd, P68 Observer II, VT-TAA, \n27.03.2021, Bhopal \n \n3 Accident M/s Jet Serve Aviation Pvt. Ltd., C90, VT-JIL, \n06.05.2021, Mumbai \n \n4 Accident Madhya Pradesh Government, B200, VT-MPQ, \n06.05.2021, Gwalior \n \n5 Accident Vistara, B737-800, VT-TGE, 07.06.2021, Mumbai-\nKolkata \n \n6 Accident M/s Indigo, ATR-72, VT-IYX, 14.06.2021, Hubli  \n7 Accident      M/s SVKM'S NMIMS Academy of Aviation Tecnam \nP2008JC, VT-BRP, Shirpur, 16.07.2021 \n(Fatal - 01) \n8 Accident M/s Indigo, ATR 72, VT-IYM, while operating flight \nfrom Tiruchirapalli to Bangalore, 04.09.2021 \n \n9 Accident M/s Red Bird Flight Training Academy, Tecnam \nP2008J, VT-RBE, Baramati, 20.09.2021. \n \n2022 \n\nS \nNo \nOccurrence \nType \n(Accident/ \nSerious \nIncident)  \nDetails of Occurrence (Airline, Aircraft \nType, Registration, Date, Place, etc.  Loss of Life \n1 Accident  M/s Pioneer Flying Academy, Cessna 172, VT-AMU, \nAligarh, 21.01.2022 \n \n2 Acciden"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |797", "t": "Khadi Gramodyog Vikas Yojana", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 797\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2023\n \n \nKHADI GRAMODYOG VIKAS YOJANA\n \n \n797. \n \n \nSHRI JAYADEV GALLA:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES be \npleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government has conducted any study regarding the implementation of the Khadi \nGramodyog Vikas Yojana (KGVY) in the country;\n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details and number of beneficiaries during the last four years, State\n-\nwise;\n \n(c) \n \nthe details of funds allocated and dispensed under the KGVY scheme to projects in each State during \nthe last four years;\n \n(d) \n \nthe details and number of work\n-\nsheds developed under the Work\n-\nshed Scheme for Khadi artisans in \nthe country, State\n-\nwise; and\n \n(e) \n \nwhether the Government has undertaken any study regarding increasing sales of khadi products \nunder the KGVY scheme in Andhra Pradesh, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERP\nRISES\n \n(SHRI BHANU PRATAP SINGH VERMA)\n \n \n(a) & (b):\n \nKhadi and Village Industries Commission\n  \n(KVIC) had conducted \nthird party Evaluation \nstudies  \nregarding the implementation of the Khadi Gramodyog Vikas Yojana (KGVY) in the country\n, the \ndetails  are as \nfollows:\n \n\n \nMott Mac Donald, Ahmadabad conducted National Level Evaluation Study of Khadi and Village \nIndustries (KVI) schemes namely Workshed Scheme for Khadi Artisans, Strengthening of \nInfrastructure of Existing Weak Khadi Institutions and Assistance for Ma\nrketing Infrastructure, \nMarket Promotion and Development assistance Scheme (MPDA), Interest Subsidy Eligibility \nCertificate (ISEC) and Science and technology ( Khadi\n \n& VI).\n \n\n \nM/s. Credit Rating and Information Service of India Limited (CRISIL), Mumbai conducted \nevaluation Study of the ‘Honey Mission and Kumhar Sashaktikaran Programme’ implemented under \nGramodyog Vikas Yojana. \n \n \nState\n-\nwise details of Cumulative Employment genera\nted under KVI sector during last four years is \nplaced at Annexure \n–\n \nI.\n \n \n(c):\n \nDetails of funds disbursed under the KGVY scheme in each State during the last four years is placed \nat Annexure\n-\nII.\n \n \n(d):\n \nState\n-\nwise details of beneficiaries benefitted under Work\nshed Scheme for Khadi Artisans during last \nfour years is placed at Annexure\n-\n \nIII.\n \n \n(e):\n \n \nThe KGVY scheme is a Central Sponsored Scheme implemented across the country with Khadi and \nVillage Industries Commission (KVIC) acting as a nodal implementing agency.\n \nThus, KVIC regularly \nconducts study regarding increasing the sales of Khadi Products under KGVY on a Pan India Level and not \nspecifically for any one state.\n \n*****\n \n\n \nAnnexure\n-\nI\n \n \nAnnexure\n-\nI referred to in reply to part \n(a) & \n(b) of the Lok Sabha Unstarred \nQuestion No. 797 for \nanswer on 07.12.2023\n \n \nState\n-\nwise details of Cumulative Employment generated under KVI sector during last four years\n \n \n(Employment : Persons in lakh)\n \nSr. No.\n \nStates / UT\n \n2019\n-\n20\n \n2020\n-\n21\n \n2021\n-\n22\