Y OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE) \n \n(a): Ministry of Housing & Urban Affairs (MoHUA) is administering \na Centrally Sponsored Scheme named “ Deendayal Antyodaya \nYojana-National Urban Livelihoods Mission (DAY -NULM)”, \nthrough the respective States/UTs, to reduce poverty and \nvulnerability of urban poor household by enabling them to  \n…2/ - \n\n-2- \naccess gainful self-employment and skilled wage employment \nopportunities, for improvement in their livelihoods on a \nsustainable basis. In addition, Prime Minister Street Vendors \nAtma Nirbhar Nidhi (PMSVANi dhi) was launched on 1 st June, \n2020 with the objective of facilitating collateral free working \ncapital loan upto Rs. 50,000/ - to street vendors, incentivis ing \nregular repayments and rewarding digital transaction. \n(b) State-wise details of funds released and utilised under DAY -\nNULM for the last five years, including the details for \nTelangana as well, are attached at Annexure-I. \n(c) Skill training  is imparted under Employment through Skills \nTraining & Placement (EST&P) component of DAY -NULM. As \nper information received from State of Telangana, 592 youths \nhave been trained during the last three years.  \n(d)&(e) DAY-NULM Management Information System Portal and Public \nFinancial Management System (PFMS) are the monitoring \nmechanism to oversee the funds allocated by t he Government \nwith the cooperation of the State Government s. Review \nMeetings through Video Conferencing/ Field visits are \nundertaken on regular basis to monitor the physical progress \nas well as utilisation of funds. \n***** \n \n \n \n  \n\nAnnexure-I \nCentral fund released and utilised during the last 5 years  \n(2018-19 to 2022-23) \n   (Rs in crore) \nSl. No States/UTs Released Utilized \n1 Andhra Pradesh 285.02 272.39 \n2 Arunachal P 19.61 15.78 \n3 Assam 89.86 82.09 \n4 Bihar 104.50 92.29 \n5 Chhattisgarh 52.88 52.88 \n6 Goa 15.55 13.58 \n7 Gujarat 198.93 189.27 \n8 Haryana 67.21 