97 \n \n              \n68 \n \n         \n94,461 \n \n31\n \n \nSindhudurg \n \n         \n26,355 \n \n           \n192 \n \n                \n2 \n \n         \n26,549 \n \n32\n \n \nSolapur \n \n      \n128,779 \n \n        \n1,741 \n \n    "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |864", "t": "Supply of Kerosene", "head": " \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 864 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 7THDECEMBER, 2023 \n \nSupply of Kerosene \n864. SHRIMATI KANIMOZHI KARUNANIDHI: \n \nपे\u0000ोिलयम और \u0000ाक ृितक गैस मं\u0000ी \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has reduced the supply of kerosene to the State of Tamil \nNadu during the last five years; \n(b)  if so, the details of kerosene supply to Tamil Nadu during the said period, year-wise; \n(c)  whether the Government is aware of the demands of Tamil Nadu Government to \nincrease the supply of kerosene; \n(d)  if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e)  the details of the steps taken by the Government to address the said demand? \n \nANSWER \nपे\u0000ोिलयम और \u0000ाक ृितक गैस मं\u0000ालय म\u0000 रा\u0000य मं\u0000ी \n(\u0000ी रामे\u0000र तेली) \n    MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PETROLEUM AND NATURAL \nGAS \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n \n(a) to (e)  Government of India makes allocation of “Public Distribution System (PDS) \nKerosene” to States/UTs including Tamil Nadu on quarterly basis for cooking and lighting \npurpose. PDS Kerosene allocation to States/UTs including Tamil Nadu have been rationalized \nsince 2010- 11 considering the polluting nature of Kerosene and taking into account, factors \nsuch as increase in domestic LPG/PNG connections, electricity coverage, non-lifting of PDS \nKerosene quota by the concerned States/UTs etc. Till date, 12 States/UTs have declared \nthemselves as Kerosene free. \nGovernment has empowered States/ UTs to draw an allocation of one month’s quota of \nPDS Kerosene at Non- Subsidized rates during each financial year for special needs such as \nNatural Calamities, Religious Functions, Fisheries, Various Yatras etc. States/UTs may seek \nfurther additional allocation after exhausting available quota.  \nRequests have been received from certain States including Tamil Nadu for increasing \nthe allocation of PDS Kerosene. Such requests are processed, after considering the factors as \nmentioned above. \n \nThe allocation of Kerosene to the State of Tamil Nadu during the last 5 years is \nannexed.  \n\nAnnexure \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to parts (a) to (e) of the Lok Sabha unstarred question No. 864 to be \nanswered on 07.12.2023 asked by Shrimati Kanimozhi Karunanidhi, on “Supply of Kerosene” \n \n(Figures in KL) \nYear PDS Kerosene  Non Subsidized PDS Kerosene \n Allocation Lapsed Quantity Allocation Lapsed Quantity \n2018-19 193776 1 17040 17040 \n2019-20 145320 1 16140 16140 \n2020-21 129168 1 12108 12108 \n2021-22 90432 1 10764 10764 \n2022-23 54240 17 7536 7536 \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |866", "t": "Creation of New Jobs in MSME Sector", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. \n866\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07.12.2023\n \n \nCREATION OF NEW JOBS IN MSME SECTOR\n \n \n866. \n \n \nSHRI RAMESH CHANDRA MAJHI:\n \n \nWill the Minister of MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM \nENTERPRISES be pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)   \n \nwhether the Government proposes to create new jobs as compensation for the loss of \nlivelihood caused due to phasing out or reducing reliance on industries like plastic and coal \n(Unsustainable Industries) and if so, \nthe details thereof; and\n \n \n \n(b)  \n \nwhether the Government proposes to ease the transition of the MSME industries involved \nin these sectors, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR MICRO, SMALL AND MEDMUM EN\nTERPRISES \n \n(SHRI BHANU PRATAP SINGH VERMA)\n \n(a) & (b):  \n \nMinistry of Micro, Small &\n \nMedium Enterprises has prepared Comprehensive \nAction Plan (CAP) and it is being implemented to ease the transition of the MSME industries \ninvolved for Phasing out of notified Single Use Plastic (SUP) items. The CAP interalia includes;  \nassistance for  set\nting up alternative enterprises through Prime Minister’s Employment \nGeneration Programme (PMEGP),  Promoting Innovations through MSME Champions Scheme, \ncreating awareness through workshops and webinars,  Marketing support through Public \nProcurement Policie\ns (PPP) for MSEs, trade fairs & exhibitions. \n \n \n \nFurther, Ministry of Coal informed that, India is augmenting its coal production for \nmeeting the increasing energy needs. Total coal consumption in India is yet to peak. Therefore, \nsome mines may close down d\nue to exhaustion of reserves but at the same time, many new coal \nmines are being operationalized to meet the growing energy demand. These mines are not only \nensuring affordability and energy security of the nation but also providing new additional \nopportun\nities for new employment and redeployment of workers in new mines from the to\n-\nbe\n-\nclosed mines to ensure better livelihood and also generate indirect employment opportunities in \ncoal regions.\n \n****\n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |867", "t": "Extension of Runway", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 867\n(To be answered on the 7th December 2023)\n \nEXTENSION OF RUNWAY\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) the bottlenecks faced by the Airports Authority of India (AAI) to extend\nthe runways and/or expand the airfields/terminals;\n(b) the details of airports which require extension of runways and expansion\nof terminals in Tamil Nadu; and\n(c) the details of new greenfield airports constructed in the country,\nparticularly in Tamil Nadu?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a): The Airports Authority of India encounters land related bottlenecks such\nas delay in handing over of land to AAI by the State Governments/Union\nTerritory Administrations/ Defence authorities, while extending the runways\nand/or expanding the airfields/ terminals.\n \n(b): The upgradation of infrastructure/facilities at airports including\nextension of runways and expansion of terminal buildings is a continuous\nprocess, which is undertaken by the Airports Authority of India (AAI) or the\nconcerned Airport Operators depending upon operational requirements,\ntraffic, demand, commercial feasibility, availability of land etc.\n \n(c): Government of India has accorded 'In-Principle' approval for setting up\nof 21 new Greenfield Airports across the country namely, Mopa in Goa, Navi\nMumbai, Shirdi and Sindhudurg in Maharashtra, Kalaburagi, Vijayapura,\nHassan and Shivamogga in Karnataka, Dabra (Gwalior) in Madhya Pradesh,\nKushinagar and Noida (Jewar) in Uttar Pradesh, Dholera and Rajkot in\nGujarat, Karaikal in Puducherry, Dagadarthi, Bhogapuram and Orvakal\n(Kurnool) in Andhra Pradesh, Durgapur in West Bengal, Pakyong in Sikkim,\nKannur in Kerala and Hollongi (Itanagar) in Arunachal Pradesh across the\n867. SHRI PARTHIBAN S.R.\n be pleased to state:-\n (GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD))\n\ncountry. Out of these, 12 Greenfield airports viz. Durgapur, Shirdi, Kannur,\nPakyong, Kalaburagi, Orvakal (Kurnool), Sindhudurg, Kushinagar, Itanagar,\nMopa, Shivamogga and Rajkot have been operationalised.\n \n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |868", "t": "Loans under PM-SVANidhi", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 868 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON DECEMBER 7, 2023 \nLOANS UNDER PM-SVANIDHI \n \nNO. 868.  SHRIMATI SUNITA DUGGAL: \n  \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to \nstate:- \n \n(a) the number of loans disbursed to beneficiaries under Pradhan \nMantri Street Vendor’s Atma Nirbhar Nidhi (PM SVANidhi), State/ \nUT-wise, particularly in the State of Haryana since its launch; \n \n(b) the amount of loan approved for female and people belonging to \nweaker sections of society such as SC/ST beneficiaries, \nparticularly in the Parliamentary Constituency of Sirsa; and \n \n(c) whether the Government has some special provisions in place/ \nplanned in regards to above mentioned beneficiaries in terms of \nrepayment of loan and if so, the details thereof? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE) \n \n(a):   As on 29.11.2023, more than 73.97 lakh loans have been \ndisbursed to 56.24 lakh beneficiaries under Pradhan Mantri Street  \n…2/ - \n\n-2- \nVendor’s Atma NirbharNidhi (PM SVANidhi) Scheme. The State/ UT -\nwise details of beneficiaries and loans disbursed including for State of \nHaryana since inception of the scheme is at Annexure-I.  \n(b): The amount of loan approved under PM SVANidhi scheme for \nfemale and people belonging to weaker sections of society such as \nSC/ST beneficiaries,  particularly in the Parliam ent Constituency of \nSirsa is at Annexure-II. \n \n(c): Yes. Under PM SVANidhi Scheme, Government is incentivizing \nregular repayment of loans through an interest subsidy of 7% per \nannum and rewarding digital transactions, by way of cash back \nupto ₹1,200 per year. These provisions are available to all \nbeneficiaries under the scheme across the country irrespective of \ntheir gender or Social status. \n*****   \n\n \nANNEXURE-I REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 868 FOR DECEMBER 07, 2023 \n  \nSTATEMENT SHOWING STATE/UT- WISE DETAILS OF BENEFICIARIES \nAND LOANS DISBURSED UNDER PM SVANIDHI SCHEME \n(As on 29.11.2023) \nS \nNo. Name of State/UT No. of \nBeneficiaries \nLoan \nDisbursed \nDisbursed \nAmount \n \n(in ₹ Crore) \n1 Andaman & Nicobar Islands 531 877 1.3 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 3,02,881 4,01,397 529.6 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 4,258 6,370 9.8 \n4 Assam 1,06,663 1,38,573 177.7 \n5 Bihar 93,642 1,15,725 141.5 \n6 Chandigarh 4,831 7,299 10.7 \n7 Chhattisgarh 69,316 96,517 131.6 \n8 Daman, Diu & Dadra & \nNagar Haveli 1,979 2,799 3.7 \n9 Delhi 1,44,122 1,67,522 195.7 \n10 Goa 1,483 2,375 3.8 \n11 Gujarat 4,12,741 5,35,021 706.8 \n12 Haryana 1,05,644 1,24,240 149.6 \n13 Himachal Pradesh 5,097 8,570 15.0 \n14 Jammu And Kashmir 15,965 23,671 35.4 \n15 Jharkhand 72,053 85,745 103.4 \n16 Karnataka 3,13,220 4,18,650 567.4 \n17 Kerala 66,318 74,752 88.9 \n18 Ladakh 411 712 1.3 \n19 Madhya Pradesh 7,29,456 10,11,021 1404.1 \n20 Maharashtra 6,66,995 7,82,013 933.1 \n21 Manipur 9,362 12,310 15.6 \n22 Meghalaya 2,349 2,958 3.8 \n23 Mizoram 1467 1774 2.3 \n24 Nagaland 2,547 3,238 4.3 \n25 Odisha 53,961 79,919 113.7 \n\nS \nNo. Name of State/UT No. of \nBeneficiaries \nLoan \nDisbursed \nDisbursed \nAmount \n \n(in ₹ Crore) \n26 Puducherry 2,986 3,955 5.4 \n27 Punjab 1,35,791 1,62,234 192.3 \n28 Rajasthan 1,28,292 1,60,101 191.9 \n29 Sikkim 935 936 0.9 \n30 Tamil Nadu 3,55,902 4,61,079 593.9 \n31 Telangana 3,99,753 6,32,255 970.0 \n32 Tripura 4,859 6,525 8.9 \n33 Uttar Pradesh 12,34,462 16,76,382 2202.2 \n34 Uttarakhand 21,843 30,111 41.7 \n35 West Bengal 1,52,497 1,59,506 165.4 \nTotal 56,24,612 73,97,132 9722.8 \n \nData Source: PM SVANidhi Portal \n \n  \n\n \nANNEXURE-II REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 868 FOR DECEMBER 07, 2023 \n  \nTHE AMOUNT OF LOAN APPROVED FOR FEMALE AND PEOPLE BELONGING \nTO WEAKER SECTIONS OF SOCIETY SUCH AS SC/ST BENEFICIARIES, AT \nNATIONAL LEVEL  AND PARTICULARLY IN THE PARLIAMENT \nCONSTITUENCY OF SIRSA UNDER PM SVANIDHI SCHEME. \n(As on 29.11.2023) \n(In ₹ in Cr.) \n \nNational Level Female SC ST OBC Minority \nAmount of Loan \nDisbursed \n4,223.72 1,848.01 291.07 4,302.56 794.37 \n \n \nSirsa \nParliamentary \nConstituency \nFemale SC ST OBC Minority \nAmount of Loan \nDisbursed \n2.63 6.22 0.03 2.44 0.08 \n \nData Source: PM SVANidhi Portal \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |869", "t": "NHs in Bihar & Haryana", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 869 \nANSWERED ON 7TH DECEMBER, 2023 \n  \nNHs IN BIHAR & HARYANA \n 869.  SHRI SUNIL KUMAR PINTU: \nSHRI RAMESH CHANDER KAUSHIK: \n  \n         Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n  \n(a) the details of funds sanctioned for Bihar, particularly Sitamarhi and \nHaryana, particularly Sonipat  for repair and maintenance of National \nHighways during the last five years till date; and \n  \n(b) the  details of the guidelines to ensure adequate illumination \narrangement and restore emergency services on National Highways? \n  \n  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \na. Details of funds sanctioned for repair & maintenance of NHs during \nlast five years including current year for the state of Bihar, \nparticularly Sitamarhi district and for the state of Haryana, \nparticularly Sonipat District are as under: \n    Fund Sanctioned (In Rs. Cr.) \nSI \nNo. \nYear Bihar Sitamarhi \nDistrict \nHaryana Sonipat  \n1 2023-24 to till date  341.50 Nil 92.54 12.63 \n\n2 2022-23 154.14 Nil 187.74 Nil \n3 2021-22 85.61 Nil 146.09 4.82 \n4 2020-21 145.73 Nil 65.35 11.00 \n5 2019-20 151.53 Nil 35.76 10.78 \n6 2018-19 190.03 Nil 48.67 Nil \nFour National Highways pass through Sitamarhi District. The \ndevelopment & maintenance works have been completed on three \nNHs during last five years and the stretches are under Defect \nLiability Period in the said District. Development of remaining NH, \nthat is   NH-527C to  2-lane with paved shoulders under \nimplementation with scheduled completion as June, 2024. \nb. Street lighting/ High mast lighting are provided in built -up / urban \nstretches and at major junctions of the National Highways as part \nof the developm ent/ upgradation of National Highways. \nRestoration of damaged National Highways to traffic worthy \ncondition is carried out through flood damage repairs/ special \nrepairs and other sub -heads of maintenance and repairs of \nNational Highways. Provision of Emerg ency services like \nAmbulance/Mobile cranes are also made through contractual \narrangements with such service providers or as part of contractual \nobligations of contractors/ concessionaires where those are \nspecified in the scope of the works.  \n***** \n             \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |87", "t": "Income Tax Returns", "head": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF REVENUE \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 87 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, DECEMBER 4, 2023/AGRAHAYANA 13, 1945 (SAKA) \n \nINCOME TAX RETURNS \n \n87. SHRIMATI MALA ROY: \n \nWill the Minister of Finance be pleased to state : \n \n(a)  the percentage of people who filed income tax returns,  paid income tax in the \nfinancial year 2022-23; \n \n(b)  the details of total amount of income tax collected  during the said financial year; \nand \n \n(c)  the annual plan and non-plan expenditure of the Income Tax Department? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF FINANCE \n(SHRI PANKAJ CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a) In Financial Year 2022 -23, 10.09 crore PAN holders have paid taxes. For the \ncorresponding period, 7.76 crore returns have been filed till 02 -12-2023 and more \nreturns are expected to be filed till the last date, i.e. 31-12-2023.  \n \n(b) The total net direct tax collection during Financial Year 2022 -23 is Rs.16,63,686.47 \ncrores out of which income tax collection is Rs.8,08,221.28 crore. \n \n(c) Starting from Financial Year 2017 -18, the classification of plan and non -plan \nexpenditure has been abolished and has been reclassified as Capital and Revenue \nExpenditure. \n \n The total expenditure of Income Tax De partment under Revenue Account is \nRs.8459.05 crore and in Capital Account is Rs.417.80 crore out of total grant \nprovisioned under Detailed Demand for Grants of Rs.9308.80 crore for the \nFinancial Year 2022-23. \n \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |870", "t": "Upgradation Work of NH 730-C", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 870 \nANSWERED ON 07TH DECEMBER, 2023 \n \nUPGRADATION WORK OF NH 730-C \n \n†870. SHRI ARUN KUMAR SAGAR \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) Whether the rehabilitation and upgradation work of National \nHighway (NH -730-C) from Farrukhabad -Allahganj-Jalalabad-Madnapur-\nKatra-Khudaganj to Pilibhit , passing through Shahjahanpur \nParliamentary Constituency of Uttar Pradesh is being carried out along \nwith two laning and paved shelter configuration in Allahganj to Miranpur \nKatra Section; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) Whether the Government has received representations for \ninvestigation by Central Technical Committee regarding alleged \nmalpractices and quality of material in the construction of the said NH; \nand \n \n(d) If so, the action taken/proposed to be taken in this regard? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n \n(a) to (b) Yes Sir, the work of  rehabilitation and upgradation  to  two \nlane and paved shoulder of National Highway 730-C from Farrukhabad-\nAllahganj-Jalalabad-Madnapur-Katra-Khudaganj to Pilibhit  in the state \nof Uttar Pradesh, totaling to 183 km in four packages , has been taken \nup under Green National Highways Corridor Project (GNHCP) with loan \n\nassistance of World Bank on Engineering, Procurement, and \nConstruction (EPC) mode. The details are placed at Annexure. \n(c)  to (d)  Yes Sir,   the Government received a representation from the \npublic representative  regarding quality issue s of works on this road \nsection .  A n   independent expert for quality a udit was appointed to \ninvestigate the alleged irregularities  in the construction and quality of \nthe construction.  Report has been submitted by the auditor to Ministry, \nwherein it is concluded that overall executed construction works are \nfound satisfactory. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) to (b) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.870 ANSWERED ON 07TH DECEMBER, 2023 ASKED BY \nSHRI ARUN KUMAR SAGAR, REGARDING “UPGRADATION WORK OF NH 730-C” \nSr. \nNo. \nNH \nNo. \nName of \nWork \nLength \n(in km) \nContract \nValue \n(Rs. in  \nCrore) \nDate of \nStart \nScheduled \nDate of \nCompletion \nPhysical \nProgress \n(till Nov-\n23)  \n(in %) \n1 NH-\n730C \nBewar-\nAllahganj \nSection of \nNH-730C \n(Km 0.000 \nto Km \n52.770) \n(Package-I)  \n52.77 196.96 24.11.2022 23.11.2024 43% \n2 NH-\n730C \nAllahganj-\nMiranpur \nKatra \nSection of \nNH-730C \n(Km 52.770 \nto Km \n114.000) \n(Package-II)  \n61.23 195.07 08.07.2022 07.07.2024 71% \n3 NH-\n730C \nMiranpur \nKatra to \nRadhaita \nSection of \nNH-730C \n(Km \n114.000 to \nKm \n137.250) \n(Package-\nIII)  \n23.25 112.41 28.07.2022 27.07.2024 39% \n4 \nNH-\n730C\n, \n730B \n& \n731K \nRadhaita to \nPilibhit \nSection \n(Package-\nIV)  \n46.13 128.88 16.08.2022 15.02.2024 54% \n  Total 183 633    \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |871", "t": "Granting Status of NH", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 871 \nANSWERED ON 7TH DECEMBER, 2023 \n  \nGRANTING STATUS OF NH  \n  \n871.   SHRI SAPTAGIRI SANKAR ULAKA: \n \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहनऔि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government proposes to grant the status of National Highways (NHs) to Bhawanipatna \nMuniguda-Bissamcuttack-Rayagada-Parvatipuram-Vizianagaram stretches;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; \n(c) whether the Government also proposes to grant NH status to Gunupur - Baliguda (Phulbani) via \nPadmapur-Gudari-Chandrapur stretch; \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and \n(e) the steps taken by the Government to upgrade the said State Highways into NHs? \n  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI)  \n  \n(a) to (e) :  Ministry receives proposals from various State Governments/UTs, public representatives, etc. for \ndeclaration/up-gradation of State roads as National Highways (NHs). Ministry considers declaration of some of the \nState roads (including in principle NHs) as NHs from time to time based on the requirements of connectivity, traffic \nlevels, inter-se priority and availability of resources subject to fulfilment of criteria for declaration as new NHs. \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |872", "t": "Scholarship Schemes for Minorities", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.872 \nANSWERED ON 07.12.2023 \n  \nSCHOLARSHIP SCHEMES FOR MINORITIES \n  \n872.     SHRI HAJI FAZLUR REHMAN: \n  \n  \nWill the Minister of MINORITY AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the details of the steps taken/proposed to be taken by the Government for welfare of \nminorities in the country; \n(b) whether various scholarship schemes meant for minorities have been implemented in all \nthe States of the country; and \n(c) if so, the details thereof including the number of students benefitted so far by the said \nschemes, State-wise? \n              \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF MINORITY AFFAIRS \n(SHRIMATI SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n  \n(a) to (c): The Government has been implementing various schemes for the welfare and \nupliftment of every strata, including minorities, especially the economically weaker and \nlesser privileged sections of the society, through different Ministries/Departments. Ministry \nof Minority Affairs has specifically implemented various welfare schemes, including various \nScholarship schemes, across the country for socio-economic and educational empowerment \nof the notified minority communities.  \nThe Scholarship schemes namely (i) Pre-Matric Scholarship, (ii) Post Matric Scholarship, \n(iii) Merit cum Means based Scholarship, implemented by Ministry of Minority Affairs are \nCentral Sector Schemes wherein, funds are directly transferred to the account of beneficiary. \nThe State-wise details of the number of students benefitted so far under the said schemes, are \navailable in the website of the Ministry i.e. https://www.minorityaffairs.gov.in. \n  \n ***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |873", "t": "Upgradation to NHs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 873 \nANSWERED ON 7TH DECEMBER, 2023 \n  \nUPGRADATION TO NHS \n 873. SHRI AJAY KUMAR MANDAL: \n  \n        Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n  \n(a) whether the Ministry is responsible mainly for the development and \nmaintenance of National Highways (NHs); \n(b) if so, the NH -wise details of the funds released and spent for the \nmaintenance on the National Highways in Bhagalpur Parliamentary \nconstituency; \n(c) whether the Vikramshila Setu constructed on the river Ganga in \nBhagalpur Parliamentary constituency is the part of NH; \n(d)  if so, the reasons for not approving the proposals for maintenance \nof the said setu on NH in Bhagalpur; and \n(e) the time since when the maintenance of the said setu has been \npending? \n  \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n  \na.  Yes, Sir. \nb. The funds for maintenance of the National Highways are released \nState-wise and not NH -wise. Details of the funds   spent  for the \nmaintenance of  National Highways passing   fully or partly in \nBhagalpur Parliamentary constituency   during last five years  are \nas under: \n\nSl. \nNo \nOld NH No. Funds Spent \n(In Rs. Cr.) \n1 106  0.74 \n2 80 33.14 \n3 133E 2.1 \n  \nc.  Yes, Sir. \nd.  & (e) It was decided at the time of sanction of construction of new \nVikramshila Bridge that the existing old 2 -lane Vikramshila Setu \nincluding whole approach road would be maintained by the State \nGovernment of Bihar from their own resources and accordingl y it \nis maintained by Government of Bihar. \n***** \n  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |874", "t": "NH-744 Greenfield Highway", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 874 \nANSWERED ON 7TH DECEMBER, 2023 \n  \nNH-744 GREENFIELD HIGHWAY \n  \n874. SHRI N.K. PREMACHANDRAN: \n \n Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to construct the NH -744 Green Field \n Highway in Kollam Lok Sabha Constituency in a time bound manner; \n \n(b) if so, the details of action taken thereon; \n \n(c) the details of funds estimated for the project construction of Green Field \n Highway NH-744 in Kollam; \n \n(d) the details of action taken to complete the land acquisition process for \n developing NH -744 Green Field Highway in Kollam Lok Sabha \n Constituency; \n \n(e) the reasons for delay in disbursing compensation for land acquisition; \n \n(f) the details of the State Government’s 25 per cent share for land \n acquisition; \n \n(g) whether the Union Government has requested for GST and royalty \n exemption for NH-744 Green Field Highway; and \n \n(h) whether the Government proposes further proceedings where the period \n of 3a notification has expired and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n\n  \n \n(a) to (d)     Yes Sir, The proposal to develop Kadambattukonam -TN/KL border \nsection of NH-744 in Kollam & Thiruvananthapuram District in Kerela is part of \nBharatmala Pariyojana with total capital cost of Rs 2570 Crore. \n \n(e) to (h)    Govt. of Kerala has requested Ministry to exempt them from sharing \n25% land Cost for the Project. On this, Ministry has requested Govt. of Kerala \nto exempt state GST and royalty for the said project. Reply to same is awaited \nfrom Govt. of Kerala. \n  \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |875", "t": "NH Fee Determination Rules on NH", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 875 \nANSWERED ON 07TH DECEMBER, 2023 \nNH FEE DETERMINATION RULES ON NH \n875. SHRI RAVIKUMAR D.: \n         \nWill the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहन औि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) the details and number of toll plazas in Tamil Nadu which are \nviolating the provisions of the National Highways Fee (Determination of \nRates and Collection) Rules 2008 regarding in distance between two toll \nplazas of 60 Kms.; \n(b) the steps taken by NHAI to close down such illegal toll plazas in \nTamil Nadu; \n(c) whether the Moratandi toll plaza on Puducherry-Tindivanam Highway \nis violating the said rule and if so, the details thereof; \n(d) whether the toll plaza was declared illegal by the Vanur Munsif Court \nin 2019 and an interim stay was obtained by NHAI citing financial loss \nto the contractor; and \n(e) if so, the details of action taken by the Government to close down \nthe said toll plaza? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI) \n\n(a) & (b) While National Highways(NH) Fee Rules, 2008 provide for \nspacing of fee plaza of 60 Kms. on same section of National Highway in \nsame direction, it also provides for establishing another fee plaza within \n60 Km, if deemed necessary by recording the reasons. While finalising \nthe location of fee plaza for a particular stretch, various aspects \nincluding the influence length under a particular fee plaza, location of \nsucceeding and preced ing fee plaza on the same stretch and in the \nvicinity, financial burden on the road users etc., are considered & \naccordingly, approval of competent authority has been taken for \nestablishment of each fee plaza. Hence, toll plazas of National \nHighways Authority of India in Tamil Nadu do not violate the provisions \nof National Highways Fee Rules. \n(c) No, Sir. Moratandi toll plaza has been established as per provision of \nNH Fee Rules as stated above. \n(d) & (e) The Hon’ble High court of Madras vide Order dated 08 .02.2019 \ngranted interim stay on the order of Vanur Munsif Court and the case \nhas subsequently been dismissed on 14.12.2021. \n*** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |876", "t": "Margin for Petroleum Dealers", "head": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 876 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 07 DECEMBER, 2023 \nMargin for Petroleum Dealers \n876. SHRI RAJMOHAN UNNITHAN: \nपे\u0000ो\u0000लयम  और \u0000ाक ृ \u0000तक गैस मं\u0000ी  \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details and number of times the Public Sector Oil Marketing Companies (OMCs) had \nhiked the dealer margin for petroleum dealers during the last six years; and  \n(b) if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \n \nपे\u0000ो\u0000लयम  और \u0000ाक ृ \u0000तक गैस मं\u0000ालय  म\u0000 रा\u0000य  मं\u0000ी  \n(\u0000ी  रामे\u0000 वर तेल\u0000) \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS \n (SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n(a) & (b):  Prices of petrol and diesel have been market-determined with effect from \n26.06.2010 and 19.10.2014 respectively. Since then, the Public Sector Oil Marketing Companies \n(OMCs) take appropriate decision on pricing of petrol and diesel in line with their international \nproduct prices, exchange rate, tax structure, inland freight and other cost elements.   \nDecision regarding revision of dealers’ commission on petrol and diesel is also taken by the \nOMCs and they have revised the dealers’ margin for petrol and diesel from time to time. Last \nsuch revision has taken place in February 2019. \nx-x-x-x-x \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |877", "t": "Solar Power Capacity", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 877 \nANSWERED ON 07/12/2023 \n \nSOLAR POWER CAPACITY \n877. SHRIMATI QUEEN OJA \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n(a) whether there is any change in total solar as well as other renewable energy capacity of the \ncountry from 2013-14 to till date, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and \n(b) whether the Government proposes to use the barren land to establish solar power system and \nif so, the details thereof, State-wise? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER  \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n(a) The renewable energy installed capacity (including solar energy) has increased from                 \n81.82 GW as on 31.03.2015 to 178.98  GW as on 31.10.2023. The sector wise details are given \nat Annexure -I. \n(b) Land is under the purview of respective State Governments, and State Governments provide \nland as per their policies. \nHowever, the Solar Park scheme of Ministry encourages use of waste/non-agricultural land for \ndevelopment of Solar Parks.  \nFurther, solar power projects can be installed on barren, fallow, pastureland, marshland of \nfarmers under Component A of PM-KUSUM scheme. \n \n***** \n \n  \n\nANNEXURE-I REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTRARRED QUESTION NO. 877 FOR 07.12.2023 \nInstalled Renewable Energy Capacity (MW) (Excluding Large Hydro Power) \nSector Cumulative Achievements \n(till 31.03.2014) \nCumulative Achievements \n(as on 31.10.2023) \nWind Power 21042.58 44292.38 \nSolar Power 2821.91 72018.04 \nSmall Hydro Power 3803.68 4986.75 \nBiomass (Bagasse) \nCogeneration 7419.23 9433.56 \nBiomass (Non-bagasse) \nCogeneration 531.82 828.25 \nWaste to Power 90.58 249.74 \nWaste to Energy (Off-grid) 139.79 323.72 \nTotal 35849.59 132132.44 \n \n  "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |878", "t": "National Highways in West Bengal", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 878 \nANSWERED ON 07th DECEMBER, 2023 \n  \nNATIONAL HIGWAYS IN WEST BENGAL \n  \n878.     SHRIMATI SAJDA AHMED: \n  \n            Will the Minister of ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \nसड़क परिवहनऔि िाजमार्ग मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n(a)     the details of proposals pending with the Government for the \nsanctioning of new National Highways (NHs) in West Bengal and if so, \nthe details thereof; \n(b)     the details of the NHs that have been sanctioned and the \nprogress of work completed in West Bengal during the last three \nyears; \n(c)     whether NH-81 in West Bengal has been renamed and if so, the \ntime by which the project would be completed; \n(d)     whether the work on the Kolkata -Varanasi Expressway \ncommenced in its stretches within West Bengal and if so, the time by \nwhich the project would be completed; and \n(e)     the details of the pending works to be completed on NH-6 from \nDhulagarh to Kolaghat in West Bengal and the time by which pending \nprojects would be completed? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF ROAD TRANSPORT AND HIGHWAYS \n(SHRI NITIN JAIRAM GADKARI)  \n  \n\n(a)   Ministry receives proposals from various State \nGovernments/UTs, public representatives,  etc. for \ndeclaration/upgradation of State roads as National Highways (NHs). \nMinistry considers declaration of some of the State roads as NHs from \ntime to time based on the requirements of connectivity, traffic levels, \ninter-se priority and availability of  resources subject to fulfilment of \ncriteria for declaration of new NHs. \n(b)    Improvement and upgradation of NHs are a continuous process \nand in the last three years 47 number projects covering 243km length \nand amounting to ₹8117 Cr have been sanctioned in West Bengal and \n67 number projects covering 917km length and amounting to ₹11,285 \ncrore have been completed. \n  \n (c)     NH-81 has been renumbered as NH -31. Two projects covering \n40 km length  have been sanctioned and these projects \nhave  scheduled completion in January, 2024 and March 2024 \nrespectively.   \n  \n (d)     Preparation of DPR for the Varanasi -Ranchi-Kolkata \nExpressway has commenced on 03.07.2021.  \n  \n(e)     Some works in  Dhulhagarh-Kolaghat section of NH -6 in the \nState of West Bengal such as 0.9 km length of Main Carriageway, 6.67 \nkm length of Service Road, 5 nos. Vehicular Underpasses (VUPs) and \n1 no.   Pedestrian Underpass (PUP) could not be taken up as the \nland  free from hindrance was not made available by the State \nGovernment. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |879", "t": "JJM in Himalayan Region", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI \nDEPARTMENT OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO-879 \nANSWERED ON-07.12.2023 \n \nJJM in Himalayan Region \n \n879. SHRI JAMYANG TSERING NAMGYAL: \n \nWill the Minister of JAL SHAKTI be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government is aware that the Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM) in the Himalayan region \nis successful in all types of residences-hill, mountain, plain, rocky and extreme harsh climates and \nif so, the details thereof; \n(b) whether the JJM is suc cessful in the winter seasons in the Himalayan region and if not, the \nsolution therefor; \n(c) whether the Government has been able to manage and distribute drinking water in water crisis \nvillages in the UT of Ladakh; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI \n \n(SHRI PRAHLAD SINGH PATEL) \n \n(a) and (b) Government of India, in partnership with States/UTs including those in Himalayan \nregion, is implementing Jal Jeevan Mission (JJM), since August 2019, to make provision of tap \nwater supply to every rural household in adequate quantity (55 lpcd), of prescribed quality (BIS \n10:500) and on a regular and long -term basis. Significant progress has been made under JJM in \nHimalayan region since its inception as reported by the States/ UTs: \n(Households in Nos.) \nSr. \nNo. State Total Rural \nhouseholds \nHouseholds with \ntap water \nconnections as \non 15.08.2019 \nHouseholds with \ntap water \nconnections as on \n05.12.2023 \n increase in \nhousehold \nconnection since \nlaunch of JJM \nNos. in % Nos. in % Nos. in % \n1.       Arunachal Pradesh 2,28,921 22,796 9.96 2,19,784 96.01 1,96,988 86.05 \n2.       Himachal Pradesh 17,08,727 7,62,721 44.64 17,08,727 100 9,46,006 55.36 \n3.       Jammu & Kashmir 18,70,347 5,75,466 30.77 14,06,407 75.19 8,30,941 44.42 \n4.       Ladakh 41,962 1,414 3.37 37,392 89.11 35,978 85.74 \n5.       Sikkim 1,31,880 70,345 53.34 1,16,651 88.45 46,306 35.11 \n6.       Uttarakhand 14,54,129 1,30,325 8.96 12,62,922 86.85 11,32,597 77.89 \n\nHousehold tap connections have been given  despite having various challenges with regard to \ntopography & climatic conditions which inter alia include difficult terrain, limited water sources, \nfreezing temperatures during winters, high implementation cost, climate change etc. \n(c) and (d)  As reported by the UT of Ladakh, the UT administration has adopted various \ntechnological solutions to ensure smooth implementation of the schemes under JJM  in villages \nwhere water crisis was prevalent during previous winters . Some of the measures adopted in \nimplementation of the schemes are as under: \ni.) Special frost-resistant materials and insulation of pipes to avoid freezing of water. \n \nii.) Focus on gravity-fed systems by utilizing natural elevation changes to minimize pumping \nand energy dependence. \n \niii.) Solar-powered water pumps for addressing electricity limitations in remote areas. \n \niv.) Freeze-thaw resistant material by using specialized insulation to withstand extreme \ntemperatures. \n \nv.) Involving local communities in planning, construction, and maintenance to ensure \nownership and sustainability.  \n \nvi.) Creating awareness on bleeding of taps during winter and waste-water management. \n \n \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |88", "t": "New Companies in Bihar", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CORPORATE AFFAIRS \n \n  LOK SABHA \n UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 88 \n  ANSWERED ON MONDAY, DECEMBER 04, 2023 \nAGRAHAYANA 13, 1945 (SAKA) \n \nNEW COMPANIES IN BIHAR \n \nQUESTION \n \n88.  SHRI VIJAY KUMAR: \n          \nWill the Minister of CORPORATE AFFAIRS                                       \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has any scheme to set up new companies in \nBihar; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) the steps taken or to be taken by the Government in this regard? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF \nSTATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION; MINISTER OF STATE \n(INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE MINISTRY OF PLANNING AND MINISTER OF \nSTATE IN THE MINISTRY OF CORPORATE AFFAIRS \n \n[RAO INDERJIT SINGH] \n(a) to (c): A company can be incorporated having registered office in any State \nof the Country in accordance with the provisions of the Companies Act, 2013 \n(Act) and rules made thereunder. The  applications filed for incorporation of \ncompanies are processed centrally at Central Registration Centre (CRC) which \nhas been established for expeditious processing of such applications. During \nthe financial years 2021-22 and 2022-23, 10,776 companies were incorporated \nhaving their registered office in the State of Bihar as per information available \non MCA-21 registry.  \n****** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |880", "t": "Subsidies for Rooftop of Houses", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 880 \nANSWERED ON 07/12/2023 \n \nSUBSIDIES FOR ROOFTOP OF HOUSES \n \n880. SHRI KANUMURU RAGHU RAMA KRISHNA RAJU \n \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has given concessions/subsidies for installation of solar panel on \nthe rooftop of Houses  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof till date, State-wise \n(c) whether some States have requested the Union Government to exempt them from sharing \nthe cost of such projects and also asked to grant complete subsidy/concession \n(d)  if so, the details thereof and the action taken thereon? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER  \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n(a) & (b)The Ministry of New and Renewable Energy (MNRE) is implementing Rooftop Solar \n(RTS) Programme Phase -II, wherein, Central Financial Assistance (CFA) is being provided for \ninstallation of RTS in residential sector. The CFA admissible for general cat egory states is Rs. \n14588/kW for first 3 kW RTS capacity and Rs. 7294/kW for RTS capacity beyond 3 kW and upto \n10 kW. For special category states (North-eastern states including Sikkim, Uttarakhand, Himachal \nPradesh, UT of Jammu & Kashmir, Ladakh, Lakshadweep, and Andaman & Nicobar Islands), the \nadmissible CFA is Rs. 17662/kW for first 3 kW RTS capacity and Rs. 8831/kW for RTS capacity \nbeyond 3 kW and upto 10 kW. The Resident Welfare Associations/ Group Housing Societies \n(RWA/GHS) are also eligible to avail  CFA for RTS installation in common facilities, upto a \nmaximum of 500 kW capacity. The CFA admissible for RWA/GHS is Rs. 7294/kW in general \ncategory states and Rs. 8831/kW in special category states. The State/UT wise details of the CFA \nreleased under the programme, is attached as Annexure. \n \n(c)&(d)Under Rooftop Solar Phase -II programme, States/UTs are not obligated to provide any \nsubsidy for rooftop solar projects. However they are at liberty to provide any subsidy/CFA which \nthey used  for such projects in addition to MNRE’s CFA.  \n \n***** \n  \n\nAnnexure referred in reply to part-b of Lok Sabha unstarred question no. 880 to be \nanswered on 07.12.2023. \nTotal CFA/subsidy released under Phase -II of Rooftop Solar Program as on \n30.11.2023 \nS. No. State/UTs Total CFA released under Phase-II (In \ncrores) \n1 Andaman & Nicobar 0.4 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 4.2 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 0.0 \n4 Assam 0.4 \n5 Bihar 5.4 \n6 Chandigarh 2.1 \n7 Chhattisgarh 1.2 \n8 DNH &DD 0.0 \n9 Goa 3.6 \n10 Gujarat 2,213.1 \n11 Haryana 25.3 \n12 Himachal Pradesh 4.3 \n13 J& K 1.2 \n14 Jharkhand 0.6 \n15 Karnataka 1.7 \n16 Kerala 189.8 \n17 Ladakh 0.0 \n18 Lakshadweep 0.0 \n19 Madhya Pradesh 29.9 \n20 Maharashtra 17.8 \n21 Manipur 0.3 \n22 Meghalaya 0.0 \n23 Mizoram 0.6 \n24 Nagaland 0.0 \n25 Delhi 4.1 \n26 Odisha 2.4 \n27 Puducherry 0.0 \n28 Punjab 23.0 \n29 Rajasthan 51.8 \n30 Sikkim 0.0 \n31 Tamil Nadu 0.0 \n32 Telangana 47.4 \n33 Tripura 0.0 \n34 Uttarakhand 8.1 \n35 Uttar Pradesh 18.8 \n36 West Bengal 0.0 \n37 SECI (National Portal) 242.7 \n Total 2,900.1 \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |881", "t": "Electricity Connections under Saubhagya Scheme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF POWER \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.881 \nANSWERED ON 07.12.2023 \n \nELECTRICITY CONNECTIONS UNDER SAUBHAGYA SCHEME \n \n881.  SHRI SHYAM SINGH YADAV: \n \n Will the Minister of POWER \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the number of electricity connections provided  to all unelectrified rural \nhouseholds and poor urban  households in the district of Jaunpur since October  \n2017 under Saubhagya Scheme; and \n \n(b)  the number of unelectrified rural and urban  households in Jaunpur district \nunwilling to take electricity connections under Saubhagya Scheme? \n \nA N S W E R \n \nTHE MINISTER OF POWER AND NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY  \n \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n \n(a) :    As per SAUBHAGYA po rtal, a total of 2,04,482 nos. of households in \nJaunpur district have been electrified covering rural and urban households. \n \n(b) :  The State has reported that the data of the Households unwilling for the \nelectricity connections was not maintained under SAUBHAGYA Scheme. Further, \nfor electrification of un -electrified households only cases of un -electrified \nhouseholds (prior to SAUBHAGYA) identified before 31.03.2019 are considered \nunder Revamped Distribution Sector Scheme-RDSS. A total of 30,055 households \nhave been sanctioned for electrification in Jaunpur district under RDSS. \n \n*************** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |882", "t": "Status of Panjim Smart City Project", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 882 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON DECEMBER 07, 2023 \n \n                  STATUS OF PANJIM SMART CITY PROJECT \n \nNO.  882  SHRI COSME FRANCISCO CAITANO SARDINHA: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether Panjim Smart City project has been started; \n \n(b) if so, the time by which it is likely to be completed and the current \nstatus thereof; \n \n(c) the number of sub-projects designated under the Panjim Smart City \nplan along with funds allocated therefor, project-wise; and \n \n(d) the number of the projects stalled/delayed along with the reasons \ntherefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE  \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n(SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE) \n \n \n(a) to (d) : Government of India launched Smart Cities Mission (SCM) \non 25 June 2015.  100 Smart Cities have been selected through 4 \nrounds of competition from January 2016 to June 2018. Pan jim was \nselected for development as a Smart City in the Fa st Track Round in \nMay 2016.   \n\n-2- \nAs on  24 November 2023, of 35 projects worth ₹ 936.75 crore being \nimplemented by Imagine Panaji Smart City Development Limited, 16 \nprojects worth ₹ 341.79 crore have been completed &  19 projects \nworth ₹ 594.96 crore are at various stages of implementation. T he \nprojects designated under the Panjim Smart City plan along with funds \nallocated therefor, project-wise is provided in Annexure-I. \nThe period of implementation of SCM has been extended upto June \n2024 and all Smart Cities , including Imagine Panaji Smart City \nDevelopment Limited, are expected to complete their projects within \nthe stipulated time. \n***** \n  \n\n \nAnnexure-I in reply to parts (a) to (d) of Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 882 for \nanswer on 07.12.2023 regarding Status of Panjim Smart City Project  asked by Shri Cosme \nFrancisco Caitano Sardinha, Hon’ble MP. \n \nDetails of Projects of Imagine Panjim Smart City Development Limited \n \n(Amount in ₹  crore) \nS.No. Project SCM Cost \n1 Smart Conversion of Overhead to Underground Electrical Network - Panaji Ribander 73.75 \n2 Implementation of Smart Radios Wireless Network with Mast Towers for Panaji City  0.21 \n3 Selection of Master System Integrator for Goa Intelligent City Management System - \nPanaji City \n214.18 \n4 Flood Mitigation Measures and Construction of Flood Water Pumping Station at Mala, \nPanaji \n17.19 \n5 Internet Bandwidth Connectivity for Goa Intelligent City Management System for Panaji \n(GICMS) – DC and DR \n3.56 \n6 Upgradation of Solid Waste Management Infrastructure in Panaji City – 2 nos. of \nBiodigester Plants of 5TPD each including 5 years of Operation and Maintenance, 2 nos. \nof Composters for leaf litter and 10 nos. of Aeration system units for composting. \n6.4 \n7 Procurement of specialized vehicles for Management of various Waste Management \nworks undertaken by the Corporation of the City of Panaji (CCP) \n3.66 \n8 Procurement of equipment for operation and maintenance of sewerage network in Panaji \nCity \n0.53 \n9 Procurement of Multi-deck Vibratory Screening Machine for the Corporation of the City \nof Panaji (CCP) \n0.47 \n10 Upgradation of Pedestrian Walkways in Panaji City - Phase 1 - Heritage route from Old \nPatto Bridge to Church Square \n2.68 \n11 Smart Classrooms- enhancing ICT learning environment in Govt. Schools in the \njurisdiction of Corporation of the City of Panaji \n0.5 \n12 Pedestrian Bridge Linking Central Library and Creek 9.43 \n13 Development of Green spaces near Government Quarters, Altinho, Panaji 1.44 \n14 Landscaping for Open Spaces at Altinho Neighborhood Greens 0.96 \n15 Construction of arch bridge connecting New Mandovi River Promenade to DB Road \nover St. Inez Creek, near ESG Building, Panaji \n6.28 \n\nS.No. Project SCM Cost \n16 Smart Classrooms- Infrastructure development involving Civil and Electrical works 0.55 \n17 Restoration, Refurbishment Interior Design of Off. Premises of Imagine Panaji Smart \nCity Dev. Ltd. \n27.58 \n18 Development of Pedestrian Spine and Revitalization of Patto Area 21.5 \n19 Development of Intelligent Public Transport Infrastructure 49.92 \n20 Rejuvenation of St. Inez Nallah - Development & Improvement to Hydrodynamics, \nWater Quality & Stabilization of Banks \n41.13 \n21 Rejuvenation of St. Inez Nallah - Reconstruction and Renovation of Culverts/Bridges at \n7 nos. of locations \n9.87 \n22 Smart Parking at Miramar 6.35 \n23 24X7 Water Supply with SCADA for Panaji City 58.11 \n24 Extension of Mandovi River Promenade on either sides to create a continuous Pedestrian \nSpine from Miramar Beach to ESG Building \n40.97 \n25 Rejuvenation of Campal area of Panaji City as a Green Space with Recreation Centre \nand facility for Smart parking. \n18.05 \n26 Improvements of roads including up-gradation, augmentation, footpath, cycle track, \ndedicated utility corridor and laying of new utilities like electrical, water supply, sewage, \nOFC etc. on Engineering, Procurement  Construction ("}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |883", "t": "Barrage Project on Sakri River", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF JAL SHAKTI \nDEPARTMENT OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 883 \nANSWERED ON 07.12.2023 \nBARRAGE PROJECT ON SAKRI RIVER \n†883.    SHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR \n Will the Minister of JAL SHAKTI  be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Barrage project at Baksauti on Sakr i river in Bihar has been approved by the Central W ater \nCommission and if so, the details thereof; \n(b) whether the proposal for construction of barrage at Baksauti on Sakri river sent by the Government of Bihar is \npending with the Ministry; \n(c) whether the said project would benefit farmers of Nawada district as well as Nalanda, Sheikhpura, Lakhisarai, \nGaya and Jehanabad; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the time by which the said pending Baksauti Barrage project would be approved? \nANSWER  \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR JAL SHAKTI  \n(SHRI  BISHWESWAR TUDU ) \n(a) & (b)    Based on appraisal of pre-feasibility report submit ted by Government of Bihar, Central Water \nCommission (CWC) under this Ministry had, in the ye ar 2012, conveyed its in-principle consent for prep aration \nof detailed project report (DPR) of the Baksauti ba rrage project. Accordingly, the DPR of “Baksauti ba rrage \nscheme on river Sakri and conversion of Nata weir to a barrage on river Nata in Nawada district with suitable link \nfrom Sakri to Nata river from Baksauti barrage site ” was submitted by Government of Bihar to CWC in th e year \n2014. \nAs per appraisal norms of CWC, a copy of the DPR wa s shared for comments, if any, with the co-basin \nState of Jharkhand. However, Govt. of Jharkhand did  not agree to the project proposal, citing its requ irement of \nthe Sakri river waters for drinking/ agricultural/ industrial needs.  \nSubsequently, several meetings were held by CWC wit h the States of Bihar & Jharkhand, to facilitate \nconvergence between the two States on the project.  In the last meeting held in June, 2018, it was dec ided Bihar \nwould recast the DPR restricting the surface water utilization from Sakri sub-basin to 159.2 million c ubic meter \n(MCM). The balance water requirement for the projec t was proposed to be met through 75% monsoon yield of \nNata river (16.59 MCM) at existing Nata weir, and t hrough conjunctive use. However, Government of Biha r is \nyet to submit the re-casted DPR to CWC for appraisal.  \n(c) & (d)    As per the information submitted in the DPR, the pr oposed project envisaged irrigation benefits in \nNawada, Jamui&Sheikhpura districts of Bihar. \nFurther, CWC guidelines for appraisal indicate a ti me span of 4-6 months for appraisal of major/ mediu m \nirrigation projects, provided the DPR is per CWC no rms, and the compliances / additional information s ought by \nCWC during appraisal are provided promptly by the S tate Government. However, as mentioned above, the r e-\ncasted DPR for the project is yet to be submitted by Government of Bihar.   \n ***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|14|UNSTARRED |884", "t": "Development of Hydro Power Projects", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF POWER \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.884 \nANSWERED ON 07.12.2023 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF HYDRO POWER PROJECTS \n \n884. SHRI SUNIL KUMAR MONDAL: \n \n Will the Minister of POWER \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government has established any  new hydro power project or \nhas developed the existing hydro power projects across the country  especially \nin West Bengal during the last two years and the current year; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof along with action  taken or being taken and \nfuturistic plans made in this  regard, State/UT -wise including West Bengal \nespecially in Bardhaman Purba constituency; and \n \n(c)  if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nA N S W E R \n \nTHE MINISTER OF POWER AND NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY  \n \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n \n(a) to (c) :  Four hydro electric projects and one Unit of Naitwar Mori  totaling  \nto 543 MW have been commissioned in the country during the last two years. \nState/UT-wise details are enclosed at Annexure-I.  Further, 42 projects of about \n18,000 MW are currently under construction. State/UT wise details are enclosed \nat Annexure-II.   \n  \n  No hydro electric project above 25 MW has been commissioned \nduring the last 2 years in the state o f West Bengal.  However, Rammam -III \nproject of 120 MW is currently under construction, Turga Pumped Storage \nProject of 1000 MW has been concurred by the Central Electricity Authority and \nis to be taken up for construction.  Teesta Intermediate hydro projec t of 90 MW \nis under survey and investigation in the state of West Bengal.  \n \n \n.........2. \n \n\n- 2 - \n \n  The Government of India has taken various policy measures \nto address the issues faced by hydro projects, which would help in development \nof hydro power proje cts in the country, including in the state of West Bengal. \nSome of the measures taken are as under: \n \ni. Declaration of  large hydro power projects (greater than 25 MW) as \nrenewable energy source \n \nii. Notification of  hydro purchase obligation  \niii. Waiver of Inter Sta te Transmission System charges for Hydro Power \nProjects and Pumped Storage projects \n \niv. Tariff rationalization measures for bringing down the tariff during the \ninitial years  \n \nv. Budgetary support for flood moderation component of hydro power \nprojects \nvi. Budgetary support for construction of enabling infrastructure, i.e. \nroads/bridges \n \nvii. Empanelment of Independent Engineer and Conciliation Committee of \nIndependent Experts for resolution of contractual disputes in hydro power \nprojects \n \nviii. Issuance of guidelines on 10.04.2 023 for promotion of  Pumped Storage \nProjects  \n \n********* \n  \n\n \nANNEXURE-I \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 884 ANSWERED IN THE LOK SABHA ON \n07.12.2023 \n************* \n  \n HYD